00:07:55,930 --> 00:07:58,031
Brazil has just passed a special tax

239
00:07:58,031 --> 00:08:00,731
deal to win data centers anyway.

240
00:08:05,183 --> 00:08:08,363
Let me draw what Nia actually learned.

241
00:08:08,473 --> 00:08:10,168
The price on the map is only

242
00:08:10,168 --> 00:08:11,303
the first block.

243
00:08:11,303 --> 00:08:13,070
Stack on top of it the wires

244
00:08:13,070 --> 00:08:14,594
to bring the power in,

245
00:08:14,594 --> 00:08:16,339
then the taxes and charges,

246
00:08:16,339 --> 00:08:17,422
then the cooling,

247
00:08:17,422 --> 00:08:19,630
then the distance to the people using

248
00:08:19,630 --> 00:08:20,893
the answers.

249
00:08:20,953 --> 00:08:22,425
And under all of it,

250
00:08:22,425 --> 00:08:23,896
the hardest one to see,

251
00:08:23,896 --> 00:08:24,923
the wait.

252
00:08:24,943 --> 00:08:27,254
A cheap power plant behind a full

253
00:08:27,254 --> 00:08:29,051
grid is like an oil field with

254
00:08:29,051 --> 00:08:30,679
no pipeline.

255
00:08:30,917 --> 00:08:33,157
And the wait can be the biggest

256
00:08:33,157 --> 00:08:34,597
