290
00:09:35,083 --> 00:09:36,056
And then,

291
00:09:36,056 --> 00:09:37,663
politics.

292
00:09:37,693 --> 00:09:39,262
When power is cheap,

293
00:09:39,262 --> 00:09:41,723
voters notice who gets it.

294
00:09:41,963 --> 00:09:45,143
Norway moved to block new crypto mines.

295
00:09:45,163 --> 00:09:47,613
Quebec decides who plugs in.

296
00:09:47,923 --> 00:09:50,225
Ireland makes newcomers bring their own

297
00:09:50,225 --> 00:09:51,243
power.

298
00:09:51,433 --> 00:09:53,976
Texas passed a law letting the grid

299
00:09:53,976 --> 00:09:56,011
tell giant users to cut back in

300
00:09:56,011 --> 00:09:57,883
an emergency.

301
00:09:58,223 --> 00:10:00,000
Cheap electricity,

302
00:10:00,000 --> 00:10:01,004
it turns out,

303
00:10:01,004 --> 00:10:03,296
is a resource governments guard,

304
00:10:03,296 --> 00:10:04,669
just like oil.

305
00:10:09,117 --> 00:10:11,797
Let me draw the big difference.

306
00:10:12,017 --> 00:10:14,567
Oil made one world market.

307
00:10:14,697 --> 00:10:17,038
A barrel costs roughly the same wherever

308
00:10:17,038 --> 00:10:17,868
you buy it,

309
00:10:17,868 --> 00:10:19,107
plus shipping.

310
00:10:19,117 --> 00:10:21,588
So oil money flowed to whoever owned

311
00:10:21,588 --> 00:10:22,637
the wells.

312
00:10:22,867 --> 00:10:25,686
Electricity makes lots of little local

313
00:10:25,686 --> 00:10:26,315
markets,

314
00:10:26,315 --> 00:10:28,867
each one stuck behind its own wires.

315
00:10:28,977 --> 00:10:30,628
So the prize doesn't go to whoever

316
00:10:30,628 --> 00:10:32,467
has the most energy.

317
00:10:32,487 --> 00:10:35,151
It goes to whoever can deliver it

318
00:10:35,151 --> 00:10:35,657
fast,

319
00:10:35,657 --> 00:10:36,696
in huge blocks,

320
00:10:36,696 --> 00:10:38,361
and keep it on.

321
00:10:38,617 --> 00:10:39,033
So,

322
00:10:39,033 --> 00:10:41,438
could cheap electricity become the new

323
00:10:41,438 --> 00:10:42,217
oil?

324
00:10:42,217 --> 00:10:43,299
In one way,

325
00:10:43,299 --> 00:10:44,127
yes.

326
00:10:44,127 --> 00:10:46,580
Just like oil a century ago,

327
00:10:46,580 --> 00:10:48,563
it's deciding where the next giant

328
00:10:48,563 --> 00:10:49,777
industries land,

329
00:10:49,777 --> 00:10:52,504
and countries are already competing for

330
00:10:52,504 --> 00:10:53,470
them with dams,

331
00:10:53,470 --> 00:10:55,557
solar fields and tax deals.

332
00:10:55,687 --> 00:10:56,525
But in another way,

333
00:10:56,525 --> 00:10:56,857
no.

334
00:10:56,857 --> 00:10:59,957
Oil could be shipped to anyone.

335
00:10:59,987 --> 00:11:01,955
Electricity has to be used close to

336
00:11:01,955 --> 00:11:02,927
where it's made.

337
00:11:02,927 --> 00:11:04,716
So the new oil isn't just cheap

338
00:11:04,716 --> 00:11:05,827
power.

339
00:11:05,857 --> 00:11:07,904
It's cheap power you can plug into

340
00:11:07,904 --> 00:11:08,337
now,

341
00:11:08,337 --> 00:11:10,384
and that a country is willing to

342
00:11:10,384 --> 00:11:11,211
share.

343
00:11:11,450 --> 00:11:14,530
So who's winning right now?

344
00:11:14,700 --> 00:11:16,505
The cold hydro north,

345
00:11:16,505 --> 00:11:18,940
for the giant training halls.

346
00:11:19,180 --> 00:11:19,846
Texas and the Gulf,

347
00:11:19,846 --> 00:11:20,730
for speed and scale.

348
00:11:20,730 --> 00:11:21,847
Quebec,

349
00:11:21,847 --> 00:11:25,530
if you can get its permission.

350
00:11:25,610 --> 00:11:26,201
Brazil,

351
00:11:26,201 --> 00:11:27,832
if it can make its power bill

352
00:11:27,832 --> 00:11:28,840
lighter.

353
00:11:29,010 --> 00:11:30,470
And the losers?

354
00:11:30,480 --> 00:11:32,996
Places with cheap power and a grid

355
00:11:32,996 --> 00:11:35,273
that can't take one more plug.

356
00:11:35,517 --> 00:11:37,667
Nia files her report.

357
00:11:37,667 --> 00:11:38,640
Not one pin,

358
00:11:38,640 --> 00:11:40,227
but a pattern.

359
00:11:40,227 --> 00:11:42,753
The giant training halls go where power

360
00:11:42,753 --> 00:11:45,317
is cheap and cold air is free.

361
00:11:45,347 --> 00:11:47,147
The answering machines stay near the

362
00:11:47,147 --> 00:11:48,007
cities.

363
00:11:48,007 --> 00:11:50,039
And the winners are the places that

364
00:11:50,039 --> 00:11:52,897
build wires as fast as data centers.

365
00:11:52,997 --> 00:11:55,197
Cubby finally gets its plug.

366
00:11:55,197 --> 00:11:57,887
And Nia gets her next assignment.

367
00:11:57,887 --> 00:12:01,033
Find the plug for the robot factories.

368
00:12:01,283 --> 00:12:01,942
Next time,

369
00:12:01,942 --> 00:12:04,895
we follow the money behind another hidden

370
00:12:04,895 --> 00:12:07,303
link of the world economy.

371
00:12:07,303 --> 00:12:09,674
This is The Hidden Economics.
